 "kind": "definition",
 "title": "The small Zariski site",
 "statement": "For a scheme $X$,\nthe site $X_{\\rm Zar}$ has its open subschemes as objects,\ninclusions as morphisms, and jointly surjective open families\nas coverings. An abelian sheaf on this site assigns abelian\ngroups to opens and satisfies the usual gluing and uniqueness\naxioms for an open covering.",
